"Fix sign of temporary offset restore in sweep_along_curve"
by Tiago Azevedo, 2026-05-29 -- landed after the 0.8.5 release.

The temporary-offset workaround subtracts the directrix centroid so the
sweep is built near the origin, then must add it back. The restore negated
the sign, placing the swept solid at -mean -- mirrored through the origin.
Only bites geometry far from the origin.

0.8.5 ships this bug AND the test that catches it: test_pipe_12d expects
min (288.98, 582.05, 118.71) and unpatched 0.8.5 gives (-290.18, -583.05,
-119.06). Verified independent of OCCT version and of occt8.patch --
unpatched 0.8.5 on OCCT 7.7.2 reproduces the identical wrong numbers, and
with this one line it produces the expected ones exactly.

--- a/src/ifcgeom/kernels/opencascade/sweep_along_curve.cpp
+++ b/src/ifcgeom/kernels/opencascade/sweep_along_curve.cpp
@@ -301,7 +301,11 @@
 
 	if (applied_temporary_offset) {
         gp_Trsf trsf;
-        trsf.SetTranslation(gp_Vec(-mean.x(), -mean.y(), -mean.z()));
+        // Restore original position: add back the mean subtracted from the
+        // directrix points above. Previously negated, which placed the swept
+        // solid at -mean instead of its original location for geometry far
+        // from the origin.
+        trsf.SetTranslation(gp_Vec(mean.x(), mean.y(), mean.z()));
         result.Move(trsf);
     }
 
